{"author":"mellosouls","children":[{"author":"kevinlu1248","children":[{"author":"mellosouls","children":[],"created_at":"2023-08-01T11:07:01.000Z","created_at_i":1690888021,"id":36954612,"options":[],"parent_id":36954244,"points":null,"story_id":36948403,"text":"Thanks for the clarification.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2023-08-01T10:01:49.000Z","created_at_i":1690884109,"id":36954244,"options":[],"parent_id":36953720,"points":null,"story_id":36948403,"text":"Thanks! The repo is just the backend that runs the GitHub webhooks. We used to have a &quot;chat with your code&quot; client but stopped supporting it. Now it&#x27;s only the GitHub interface with creating tickets and comments.","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}],"created_at":"2023-08-01T08:28:06.000Z","created_at_i":1690878486,"id":36953720,"options":[],"parent_id":36948403,"points":null,"story_id":36948403,"text":"OT: I&#x27;m not clear on whether or not Sweep is fully open source - I mean, can you run it fully self-hosted (apart from the GPT4 engine obv), or is the repo essentially a client to a Sweep API&#x2F;binary?<p>Cool project btw!","title":null,"type":"comment","url":null}
